<table>
<tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Exception</th><th>Error</th></tr>
<tr><td>Usually caused by</td><td>Our program (programmatic mistake)</td><td>NOT our program — lack of system resources</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recoverable?</td><td>Yes (recoverable)</td><td>No (non-recoverable)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Programmer action</td><td>Can often catch and recover</td><td>Cannot fix in code — need admin / more memory</td></tr>
<tr><td>Examples</td><td>FileNotFoundException, ArithmeticException</td><td>OutOfMemoryError, StackOverflowError</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th></th><th>Exception</th><th>Error</th></tr>
<tr><td>Cause</td><td>Program logic / environment interaction we coded</td><td>JVM / system resource exhaustion</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fix</td><td>Fix code or catch + alternate path</td><td>Increase memory, fix recursion, JVM tuning</td></tr>
<tr><td>Catch in practice?</td><td>Yes (try-catch)</td><td>Theoretically catchable but should not treat as recoverable</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Direct child of Exception</th><th>Notable grandchildren</th></tr>
<tr><td>`RuntimeException`</td><td>ArithmeticException, NullPointerException, ClassCastException, ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException, StringIndexOutOfBoundsException, IllegalArgumentException, NumberFormatException</td></tr>
<tr><td>`IOException`</td><td>EOFException, `FileNotFoundException`, InterruptedIOException</td></tr>
<tr><td>`SQLException`</td><td>(database errors)</td></tr>
<tr><td>`ServletException`</td><td>(web)</td></tr>
<tr><td>`RemoteException`</td><td>(RMI)</td></tr>
<tr><td>`InterruptedException`</td><td>(thread interrupt)</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Direct child of Error</th><th>Notable grandchildren</th></tr>
<tr><td>`VirtualMachineError`</td><td>`StackOverflowError`, `OutOfMemoryError`</td></tr>
<tr><td>`AssertionError`</td><td>(failed assert statements)</td></tr>
<tr><td>`ExceptionInInitializerError`</td><td>(static/instance initializer block failure)</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Statement</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Method where exception is raised creates Exception object (name, description, location/stack trace).</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>That method hands object to JVM.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>JVM checks for handling code in that method; if absent → abnormal termination + pop stack.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>JVM checks caller method; same rule → terminate + pop if no handler.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Repeat until `main`.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>If `main` has no handler → terminate main + pop; JVM gives object to Default Exception Handler.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Default handler prints exception info → abnormal program termination.</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th></th><th>Exception</th><th>Error</th></tr>
<tr><td>Root parent</td><td>Throwable</td><td>Throwable</td></tr>
<tr><td>Typical cause</td><td>Programmer / application logic</td><td>System resources / JVM limits</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recoverable</td><td>Yes (e.g. fallback file)</td><td>No (increase heap, fix environment)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Examples</td><td>FileNotFoundException, ArithmeticException</td><td>OutOfMemoryError, StackOverflowError</td></tr>
</table>
